<main class="detail-page"><a class="back-link" href="cars.html">← Back to the cars</a><section class="detail-hero image-m5"><div class="detail-title"><p class="eyebrow">BMW M · F90 · LIMITED-RUN PERFORMANCE SALOON</p><h1>BMW M5 <span>CS</span></h1><p>Comfort for the journey. Focus for the fast road.</p></div></section>
<section class="detail-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE STORY</p><h2>The most focused F90 M5.</h2></div><div><p>The M5 CS takes the F90-generation M5 and turns up its sharper side. Its twin-turbo V8 sends power to all four wheels through BMW’s M xDrive system, while a weight-saving programme, chassis changes, and distinctive carbon-fibre details give the CS a more purposeful feel. It remains a four-door saloon with rear seats, so the performance comes with real everyday usability.</p><p>BMW announced the car in 2021. It was a 2022 model year car in the US and was offered in Europe from 2021; there was no 2023 model-year F90 M5 CS.</p></div></section>
<section class="spec-section"><p class="eyebrow">KEY FIGURES · EUROPEAN SPECIFICATION UNLESS NOTED</p><h2>At a glance</h2><div class="spec-grid"><div class="spec"><strong>4.4L V8</strong><span>Twin-turbo petrol</span></div><div class="spec"><strong>635 PS</strong><span>European output · 627 hp US</span></div><div class="spec"><strong>750 Nm</strong><span>Peak torque</span></div><div class="spec"><strong>3.0 sec</strong><span>0–62 mph (0–100 km/h)</span></div><div class="spec"><strong>189 mph</strong><span>Top speed · approx. 305 km/h</span></div><div class="spec"><strong>8-speed</strong><span>M Steptronic automatic</span></div><div class="spec"><strong>M xDrive</strong><span>Switchable all-wheel drive</span></div><div class="spec"><strong>£140,780</strong><span>Original UK on-the-road price</span></div></div></section>
<section class="detail-copy"><h2>What makes it special?</h2><div class="copy-grid"><article><h3>More power, less weight</h3><p>The 4.4-litre V8 produces 635 PS in European trim. BMW used carbon-fibre-reinforced plastic for parts such as the bonnet and exterior trim and reduced weight by about 70 kg compared with the M5 Competition in the European press information.</p></article><article><h3>Four-seat focus</h3><p>Distinctive M Carbon bucket seats are fitted in front, with two individual rear seats. The cabin keeps the comfort and technology expected of an M5 while giving the CS a more special, driver-focused atmosphere.</p></article><article><h3>Road and track ability</h3><p>M xDrive helps put the power down, and the chassis receives CS-specific tuning. BMW quoted 0–100 km/h in 3.0 seconds and a 305 km/h top speed for the European car.</p></article><article><h3>Price note</h3><p>The £140,780 figure is the original UK on-the-road list price, not a current used-market valuation. Present-day prices depend on condition, mileage, specification, and country.</p></article></div></section>
